   "project": "fieldnotes",
   "reply": "`list` follows the ISO-8601 rule.\n\n- **Where the date comes from:** `list` (`fieldnotes/cli.py:21`) prints `note['created']` as it is stored. It does no date formatting of its own.\n- **How it's stored:** `store.add` (`fieldnotes/store.py:24`) writes `moment.isoformat()`. That gives a UTC value like `2026-01-02T03:04:05+00:00`.\n- **Other date output:** Nothing else in the code formats dates. `add` prints only the note text, and the grep found no `strftime` or locale-based formatting.\n\nI only searched the `.py` files and didn't open `README.md` or `tools/check.py`. A hand-written locale-style date in the README would be easy to miss, so check it if that matters.\n\nOne thing to be aware of: `list` prints whatever string is in `notes.json`. If an old or hand-edited file holds a non-ISO value, `list` will show it unchanged. Nothing validates or normalizes dates on load. Say so if you want a check added."
  },
