   "project": "fieldnotes",
   "reply": "I added `python -m fieldnotes.cli export`, which prints one line per note as `DATE: TEXT`. The project checks pass: both unit tests, the new one and the existing one, and the line-length rule.\n\n- **Date format:** `DATE` is the note's full stored timestamp, for example `2026-01-02T03:04:05+00:00: first`. If you wanted only the calendar date, that's a small change.\n- **Usage message:** I added `export` to the usage text.\n- **Test:** `tests/test_cli.py` adds two notes and checks that `export` returns 0 and prints the two expected lines.\n- **How I ran the checks:** `tools/check.py` needs `NOTES_HOME` set. I pointed it at a temporary directory, so no real notes were touched.\n\nThe command itself is in `fieldnotes/cli.py`."
